# SimePark environment variables — EXAMPLE FILE
#
# Copy this file to `.env` and fill in your own values:
#     cp .env.example .env
#
# `.env` and every `.env.*` file are git-ignored. Only this example file is
# committed, and it must never contain a real key.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# GEMINI_API_KEY  (server-side only — REQUIRED for the AI assistant)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Get a key from Google AI Studio: https://aistudio.google.com/apikey
#
# This variable is read ONLY by server code:
#   - api/_lib/handler.ts            (Vercel Serverless Function)
#   - server/assistantDevMiddleware.ts (local Vite dev server)
#
# It is deliberately NOT prefixed with VITE_. Vite only exposes VITE_-prefixed
# variables to the browser, so this value never reaches the client bundle.
# Do not rename it to VITE_GEMINI_API_KEY. Do not commit a real key.
GEMINI_API_KEY=your_gemini_api_key_here

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# GEMINI_MODEL  (server-side only — OPTIONAL)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Overrides which Gemini model the assistant calls. If unset, the code default
# in src/types/assistant.ts (DEFAULT_GEMINI_MODEL) is used.
#
# Model availability and free-tier limits change over time. Check the current
# list and your own quota in Google AI Studio before changing this:
#   https://ai.google.dev/gemini-api/docs/models
# A fast, low-cost Flash-class model is the right choice for this feature.
# Example value (verify it is still offered before relying on it):
# GEMINI_MODEL=gemini-3.5-flash-lite
